<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bathys Ryax</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">872 or 878</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bathys Ryax was fought in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> between the Byzantine army of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-i">Basil I</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paulicians">Paulicians</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divrigi">Tephrike</a>, probably in 872 or 878. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> surprised the Paulician army as it withdrew from a raid into imperial territory, and its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chrysocheir">Chrysocheir</a> was killed. The defeat broke Paulician power, and Tephrike fell to the Byzantines soon afterwards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bathys-ryax.jpg" alt="Battle of Bathys Ryax" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cplakidas · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Asia_Minor_ca_842_AD.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
